new_note19 = "[^19]: The 2019 correspondence inventory records Huizinga to Malinowski, 27 October 1933 [1059], incipit ‘This morning I came across a review of Hofstra’s book’, and Malinowski to Huizinga, 30 October 1933 [1060]. The book was Sjoerd Hofstra, *Differenzierungserscheinungen in einigen afrikanischen Gruppen: Ein Beitrag zur Frage der primitiven Individualität* (1933). Huizinga’s Amsterdam lecture of 6 November 1933, *Natuurbeeld en historiebeeld in de achttiende eeuw* (published in *Neophilologus* 19 [1934], pp. 81–95; *Verzamelde Werken* IV, pp. 341–359), cites Hofstra, p. 126, for W. C. Willoughby’s example of a prophet among *natuurvolken* calling people back to old loyalties and locating the ideal age in the past. The collected works places the text under the editorial heading `[Renaissance en Nieuwe Tijd]`; that heading is not the original publication title."
